course: dictionary
lesson: 14188
title: An old word for morning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to poems, songs and old stories. Morn is one of them. It is a literary word, so writers use it to sound graceful or old-fashioned. «The birds began to sing at morn.» Here morn means morning, the early part of the day.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Morn often appears in phrases like «on Christmas morn», and a hymn or poem about a special day is a clue that the writing is old-fashioned. Ask: what word would fit here? Morning fits, so morn means morning.
explain: In Scotland, people use «the morn» in everyday talk, and it means tomorrow. «Mum says, "We're going swimming the morn."» The clue is the plan: a trip that has not happened yet. Swap in a meaning to check. If the sentence is about the next day, the meaning is tomorrow.
fact: Morn means morning. It is a literary word, found mostly in poems, songs and old stories.
fact: «On Christmas morn» means on Christmas morning.
fact: In Scotland, «the morn» means tomorrow in everyday talk.
fact: Literary words make writing sound old-fashioned or poetic.
fact: Morn sounds like mourn, but they are different words: mourn means to feel deep sadness, often after someone has died.
exercise: «The birds began to sing at morn.» What does morn mean here? | Next year | *Morning | Evening | Midnight
exercise: Which word in «on Christmas morn» is the old-fashioned word for morning? | *morn | Christmas | song | on
exercise: A Scottish friend says, «We're going to the beach the morn.» When is the trip? | At midnight | Years ago | *Tomorrow | Yesterday
test: The poet wrote, «Dawn and morn bring new light to the hills.» What does morn mean? | Evening | Sunset | *Morning | Night
test: A Scottish child says, «I'll see you the morn.» When will they meet? | Right now | *Tomorrow | Yesterday | Last Christmas
exam: Why would a writer choose morn instead of morning in a poem? | It is only used on shopping lists | *It sounds old-fashioned and poetic | It means the same as night | It means the end of a game
